Under fa-IR, the date strip and the header subtitle forced
`calendar: "gregory"`, printing "۲۶ اکتبر" while the calendar sheet
rendered the same day as "۴ آبان" (Jalali). Two calendar systems on one
screen is jarring for an Iranian audience.

Fix: drop `calendar: "gregory"` from both formatters (DateStrip.tsx
fullDate, Matches.tsx headerDayFormatter) so fa-IR uses its native
Jalali calendar. Also render the chip day number via `toJalali(day).jd`
under fa-IR so the visible chip matches the sheet. The chip's
aria-label still names the same day its digits show.

EN is unchanged (Gregorian, no edits). CalendarSheet.tsx is unchanged
(already Jalali for FA). The strip's window math and `dayKey` stay
Gregorian — only the printed number changes.

Audit finding: audit-full.md, row 3 (HIGH).
Files: src/components/DateStrip.tsx, src/pages/Matches.tsx.

